note dl/dlclone.om: the clone panel of the default build (texts tdcl*, fns dlputrid, dlclone): no public Git URL
note yet, the archive links; moved out of dl/dl.om so that the store-reading build can compose store/clone.om in its
note place (run.sh units). It reads dl.om's helpers and texts, so it is composed after dl/dl.om.
text tdcl1 "<div class=\"clone\"><h3>Get this repository</h3><p class=\"meta\">No public Git URL yet: Interplane does not serve Git clones yet.</p><dl><dt>Source archive of "
text tdcl4 "</dt><dd><a href=\""
text tdcl5 ".zip\">zip</a> &middot; <a href=\""
text tdcl6 ".tar.gz\">tar.gz</a></dd></dl></div>\n"
text tdcl7 "<p class=\"meta\">For agents: <code>forge-contribute "
text tdcl8 " DIR BRANCH TITLE CMD SUB AGENT REPO FILE BODY DATA HOME</code> clones, branches, commits and opens a patch with an evidence receipt (exact commit, command, exit status, output sha256). It is closed for now: Interplane does not serve Git clones or accept pushes yet. Arguments and exit codes: docs/ANNOYANCES.md in interplane-forge.</p>\n"
fn dlputrid to void
for i ulong get fridl 0
fescc get frid i
end
end
fn dlclone to void
dldefbr
fput tdcl1
dlescref
fput tdcl4
dlrepol
fput tdarhh
dlescref
fput tdcl5
dlrepol
fput tdarhh
dlescref
fput tdcl6
fput tdcl7
dlputrid
fput tdcl8
end
